The rule is complete and verified. Here's a summary of the final rule in `/root/local.rules`:

---

### Rule Breakdown (`sid:1000001`)

```
alert http any any -> any any (
    msg:"DATA EXFIL - Custom telemetry exfiltration pattern detected";
    flow:established,to_server;
    http.method; content:"POST";
    http.uri; content:"/telemetry/v2/report"; bsize:20;
    http.header; content:"X-TLM-Mode"; nocase; content:"exfil"; distance:0; within:10;
    http.request_body; content:"blob="; content:"sig=";
    pcre:"/blob=[A-Za-z0-9+\/=]{80,}/P";
    pcre:"/sig=[0-9a-fA-F]{64}([&\s]|$)/P";
    sid:1000001; rev:1;
)
```

**How each condition maps to a detection keyword:**

| Requirement | Keyword(s) |
|---|---|
| (1) HTTP POST | `http.method; content:"POST";` |
| (2) Exact path `/telemetry/v2/report` | `http.uri; content:"/telemetry/v2/report"; bsize:20;` — `bsize:20` ensures the URI buffer is exactly 20 bytes (the length of the path), preventing partial matches on longer URIs |
| (3) Header `X-TLM-Mode: exfil` | `http.header; content:"X-TLM-Mode"; nocase;` followed by `content:"exfil"; distance:0; within:10;` — matches the header name case-insensitively, then requires `exfil` immediately after within 10 bytes (covers `: exfil`) |
| (4) Body `blob=` + Base64 ≥ 80 chars | `content:"blob=";` for fast prefilter + `pcre:"/blob=[A-Za-z0-9+\/=]{80,}/P";` validates 80+ Base64 characters after `blob=` |
| (5) Body `sig=` + exactly 64 hex chars | `content:"sig=";` for fast prefilter + `pcre:"/sig=[0-9a-fA-F]{64}([&\s]|$)/P";` validates exactly 64 hex chars followed by a delimiter or end-of-body |

**Test results:**
- `train_pos.pcap` (header: `x-tlm-mode: exfil`) — **alert fired**
- `train_neg.pcap` (header: `x-tlm-mode: normal`) — **no alert** (correct, no false positive)
